! ja_ax1a "IBOX-1", routine IBIN1-IBIN6, p.24 (octal 004023.00-
! 004031.40): "BRANCH ON I BOX INDICATORS %B-IND%", the XF group.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK.  index_result_indicators.strap pins the index RESULT
! indicators for the immediate operations, but every index word in it
! has flag 0, so XF -- the index flag indicator -- was pinned nowhere.
! This is the deck's own test of it, and being a transcription it meets
! the stronger of the two standards used in this suite.
!
! IT ALSO PINS THE BRANCH-AND-ZERO CLEAR.  The mnemonics here are the
! full grammar: a leading Z means BRANCH IF THE BIT IS OFF, a trailing
! Z means TURN THE BIT OFF after testing.  The listing's own comments
! give the truth table, and the block walks XF through both polarities
! and then clears it:
!
!   IBIN1  BZXF,$      hang up if bit off      XF on  -> no branch
!   IBIN2  BXF,$+1.0   dont branch if bit off  XF on  -> branch, over
!                                              a BD,$ "hang up if no branch"
!   IBIN3  BZXFZ,$     hang up if bit off OR TURN OFF -- no branch, and
!                                              the trailing Z clears XF
!   IBIN4  BXF,$       hang up if bit on       XF now off -> no branch
!   IBIN5  BZXF,$+1.0  branch if bit off       XF off -> branch, over
!                                              a BD,$ "hang up if bit on"
!
! So a model that never set XF hangs at IBIN1, and one that set it but
! ignored the trailing-Z clear hangs at IBIN4.  Both measured below.
!
! THE SEED IS ONE WORD.  IBXWZO is value -1, flag 1, count 0, refill 0
! -- negative, flagged and zero-count at once, which is why the listing
! calls it "COMMON XW FOR XF,XCZ,XVLZ" and reuses it for the XCZ and
! XVLZ groups that follow (not transcribed here).
!
! A DISCREPANCY IN XW's FOURTH FIELD, recorded because it is unresolved
! rather than because it matters here.  The listing writes this constant
! "XW,-1,0,0,4" and assembles flag = 1, refill = 0; jb_ax4b p.67 writes
! "I38B46 XW,0,0,0,%8=400000" and assembles refill = 0400000, flag = 0.
! Both were re-read at 400 dpi to rule out a misread.  Under any single
! field order one of them is wrong, so the two tapes appear to use
! different XW conventions -- plausibly different STRAP versions, since
! they are different programs.  C22-6531 and C28-6129 have no text layer
! to settle it.  This assembler treats the fourth field as a one-bit
! flag, so the source below writes 1 where the listing writes 4; the
! ASSEMBLED WORD is identical to the listing's, which is what the verify
! script checks.

        SLC, (8)4023.0
IBINX   LX, $X1, IBXWZO                      ! turn on XF, XCZ, XVLZ
IBIN1   BZXF, $                              ! hang up if bit off
IBIN2   BXF, $+1.0                           ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN3   BZXFZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN4   BXF, $                               ! hang up if bit on
IBIN5   BZXF, $+1.0                          ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN6                             ! branch out
IBXWZO  XW, -1, 0, 0, 1                      ! listing writes "XW,-1,0,0,4"
IBIN6   VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
PASS    BEW, $
        END, IBINX
